# Windows batch files must keep CRLF line endings to run reliably. Mark them
# as non-text so git stores the CRLF bytes verbatim — this way a GitHub
# "Download ZIP" (which ignores eol conversion) still delivers CRLF, not LF.
# (LF-ended .bat files fail on Windows with "X was unexpected at this time".)
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text

# Binary assets — never touch line endings.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
